```java
// Spring Boot 3.2 + Java 17: the framework annotations are identical,
// but Boot auto-configures DispatcherServlet, Jackson, and Tomcat.
@SpringBootApplication
public class OrderApplication {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(OrderApplication.class, args);
    }
}

@RestController                       // from spring-web (the framework!)
@RequestMapping("/api/orders")
class OrderController {
    @GetMapping
    List<Order> all() { return List.of(new Order(1L, "book")); } // returned as JSON automatically
}

record Order(Long id, String item) {}
```

Notice the controller code is pure Spring Framework — Boot only removed the `WebConfig` and `web.xml`.

